course: dictionary
lesson: 1978
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word compose is a good example. «She composed a letter to her gran» means she wrote it. «Water is composed of hydrogen and oxygen» means water is made of those two parts.
explain: Look at the words around compose before you choose a meaning. Words like music, poem and letter point to writing or creating. Words like hydrogen and oxygen point to parts. Words about feelings point to calming down. Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: «Compose yourself» is a phrase, so learn it as one piece. It means calm down, as in «she composed herself before she spoke». Here compose does not mean write at all. Phrases like this can change the meaning completely, so read the whole group of words.
fact: «Compose» means to write or create music, a poem or a letter.
fact: «Composed of» means made of parts, as in «water is composed of hydrogen and oxygen».
fact: «Compose yourself» means calm down and control your feelings.
fact: In «perhaps the most conceited song that any animal ever composed», compose means wrote or created.
fact: Ada wrote that a machine might compose music if music could be turned into numbers. Here compose means create.
exercise: «She composed a letter to her gran.» What does composed mean here? | *Wrote | Calmed down | Made of parts | Lost
exercise: «Water is composed of hydrogen and oxygen.» What does composed of mean? | Written in a book | Calm and quiet | Made of parts | *Made of parts, like water is made of two gases
exercise: «Before she spoke, she took a deep breath and composed herself.» What does composed herself mean? | Wrote a poem about her feelings | Made a machine | *Calmed down and controlled her feelings | Shouted loudly
test: The children will compose a tune in music lesson. What does compose mean? | Sing very loudly | Break into pieces | *Write or create | Fall asleep
test: Which phrase means calm down and control your feelings? | *Compose yourself | Composed of | Compose music | Compose a letter
exam: Ada wrote that the machine might compose music if music could be turned into numbers. What does compose mean here? | To be made of parts | To calm down | *To write or create | To copy exactly
